# Airbnb-clone rules

- Stack is fixed: React + TypeScript (Vite) frontend, Java 21 + Spring Boot
  backend. Do not introduce Angular or a Node backend.
- Original implementation only: match the reference page's layout/behaviour,
  never copy its source code, hashed class names, or image assets.
- All listing content flows through the Java API
  (`/api/listings/{id}`, `/quote`). Keep `frontend/src/data/listing.json`
  in sync as the offline fallback snapshot.
- Design tokens are CSS variables in `frontend/src/index.css`
  (Rausch `#ff385c`, Ink `#222222`, 1120px column). Reuse them; don't
  hard-code new colours/spacing scales.
- Overlays must be accessible dialogs: focus trap, Esc closes, focus is
  restored to the opener, body scroll is locked (`src/lib/hooks.ts`).
- Desktop only; still respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Before declaring done: backend `mvn package` and frontend `npm run build`
  must pass, and the running page must be screenshot-checked.
